@prefix : <http://mee.foundation/ontologies/cell/shapes#> .
@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix cell: <http://mee.foundation/ontologies/cell#> .
@prefix topic: <http://mee.foundation/ontologies/topic#> .
@prefix p: <http://mee.foundation/ontologies/persona#> .
@prefix o: <http://mee.foundation/ontologies/organization#> .

<http://mee.foundation/ontologies/cell/shapes> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
    owl:versionInfo "Version 3.21.0 - :ACellShape's cell:creator constraint's sh:or narrowed to p:Person/o:Organization (dropped g:Group), matching cell.ttl 3.28.0's elimination of the g:Group concept entirely; reworded the constraint's surrounding comment and sh:message accordingly. No example data affected: the one cell that ever used a g:Group creator/subject value (Boston Hub Society) never used cell:creator for it — its cell:creator was always \":Self\". (3.20.0 - :ACellShape's cell:creator constraint gained sh:minCount 1 (previously only sh:maxCount 1): cell.ttl 3.27.0 made cell:creator required (1..1, not 0..1) for every cell:ACell, since every actual cell's content is authored by someone — there is no longer a legal 'no creator' case. Reworded the constraint's surrounding comment and sh:message accordingly. No example data violates the stricter constraint: all 19 example cell-databooks typed cell:ACell already carried a valid mia.creator value (always \":Self\") before this change; cell-templates.ttl's 4 template individuals remain exempt, same as they already are for cell:subject/cell:memberTopics, since Tier 1 validation excludes cell-templates.ttl from its merged run entirely (see CLAUDE.md Check 5). (3.19.0 - :CellShape's cell:origin constraint reverted to sh:maxCount 1 only (dropped 3.18.0's sh:minCount 1): the user reconsidered and reintroduced UserDefined as a genuine third category type, meaning a cell can legally have no cell:origin again — but now with a precise trigger (its cell-databook's filename carries the literal \"(custom)\" disambiguator) rather than the old vague \"no canonical counterpart\" judgment call. That filename/origin pairing can't be expressed in SHACL (it can't see filenames), so it's checked in CLAUDE.md's Check 20/10j instead. Reworded the constraint's surrounding comment and sh:message accordingly. No example data affected: all 36 example cell-databooks already carried a valid mia.origin value both before and after this reversion. (3.18.0 - :CellShape's cell:origin constraint gained sh:minCount 1: cell.ttl 3.25.0 made cell:origin required (1..1, not 0..1) for every cell:Cell, since a category folder is defined by the presence of a matching cell-databook and every category folder's cell-databook must now carry an origin — there is no longer a legal 'no matching canonical class' absent case. Reworded the constraint's surrounding comment and sh:message accordingly. No example data violates the stricter constraint: all 36 example cell-databooks already carried a valid mia.origin value before this change. (3.17.0 - removed :CellShape's cell:folder cardinality constraint outright, matching cell.ttl 3.23.0's removal of cell:folder itself (a cell's folder is now purely the filesystem folder its cell-databook physically lives in, never a stored path — nothing left to constrain). :CellShape now constrains only cell:origin's cardinality. (3.16.0 - reworded :CellShape's cell:origin cardinality comment, which referenced cat:UserDefined and cat:category by name (category.ttl 1.31.0 deleted cat:Folder and its subclasses, along with cat:category, outright) — now describes the absent case as \"a folder with no matching canonical class\" instead. Comment-only change; no shapes, paths, or cardinalities added, removed, or altered. (3.15.0 - added a cell:origin cardinality constraint (at most one value — 0..1, matching README.md's pre-existing 'else nil for cat:UserDefined folders' description of this property) to :CellShape, matching cell.ttl 3.20.0's new cell:origin property (domain cell:Cell). Not constrained via sh:class cat:Category, since a legal value is the concrete leaf subclass itself, never rdf:type cat:Category. (3.14.0 - renamed :OnePartyShape/:TwoPartyShape/:ThreePlusPartyShape to :OneMemberShape/:TwoMemberShape/:ThreePlusMemberShape and their sh:targetClass values to cell:OneMember/cell:TwoMember/cell:ThreePlusMember, matching cell.ttl 3.17.0's cell:OneParty/cell:TwoParty/cell:ThreePlusParty -> cell:OneMember/cell:TwoMember/cell:ThreePlusMember rename; also updated :ACellShape's cell:parties/cell:partyTopics sh:path values to cell:memberCount/cell:memberTopics. No cardinality changes — a pure terminology shift. (3.13.0 - removed :CellShape's cell:note constraint (cell:note was removed from cell.ttl 3.15.0, merging the separate notes/files folder hierarchies into one under cell:folder); :CellShape now constrains only cell:folder's cardinality. 3.12.0: split cell:topics's constraint into cell:otherTopics (unbounded, uniform, stays on :ACellShape) and cell:partyTopics (required baseline, now enforced per party count by three new shapes: :OnePartyShape, :TwoPartyShape, :ThreePlusPartyShape, targeting cell:OneParty/cell:TwoParty/cell:ThreePlusParty respectively). Also moved cell:subject's minCount/maxCount off the uniform :ACellShape and onto those same three per-party shapes, tightening it from a blanket 1..2 to exactly 1 for cell:OneParty/cell:ThreePlusParty and 1..2 for cell:TwoParty — :ACellShape now only checks cell:subject's sh:nodeKind sh:IRI uniformly.))))))))"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Cell Ontology SHACL Validation Shapes"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "SHACL validation shapes for cell:Cell DataBook instances (the content facet of a cell) in the Cell Ontology."@en .


#################################################################
#  Cell
#  cell:Cell (formerly cell:Parties) carries only what's common to
#  every cell regardless of facet: origin (cell:folder was removed
#  outright in cell.ttl 3.23.0 — a cell's folder is now purely the
#  filesystem folder its cell-databook physically lives in, never a
#  stored path, so there's nothing left to constrain here). Identity/
#  topic links (cell:subject/cell:memberTopics/cell:otherTopics) live
#  on :ACellShape and the per-member-count shapes below, since their
#  domain narrowed from cell:Cell to cell:ACell in cell.ttl 3.10.0 —
#  a cell not yet typed cell:ACell has none of them.
#################################################################

:CellShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass cell:Cell ;
    sh:message "Cell validation."@en ;

    # cell:origin — at most one value (0..1, cell.ttl 3.26.0), on any
    # cell:Cell regardless of facet. Absent exactly when the cell is of
    # the UserDefined category — identified precisely by its
    # cell-databook's filename carrying the literal "(custom)"
    # disambiguator, not a vague "no canonical counterpart" judgment
    # call; SHACL can't see filenames, so this specific absence/filename
    # pairing is checked in CLAUDE.md's Check 20/10j, not here. Not
    # constrained via sh:class cat:Category: a legal value is the
    # concrete leaf subclass itself (e.g. cat:Others), never rdf:type
    # cat:Category — class-value punning, same reasoning as
    # cell:memberCount's range below.
    sh:property [
        sh:path cell:origin ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:message "A cell may have at most one cell:origin value: the cat:Category subclass its content is filed under, if any."@en
    ] .


#################################################################
#  TCell
#  cell:TCell is the template facet of a cell (cell.ttl 3.7.0) —
#  reusable content reached via a cat:Category subclass's
#  cat:templateCell (category.ttl).
#################################################################

:TCellShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass cell:TCell ;
    sh:message "Template Cell validation."@en ;

    # cell:templateShape — at most one value. Not constrained to sh:class
    # sh:NodeShape here: the individuals it points at (e.g.
    # pshapes:PassportDocumentShape) are only typed sh:NodeShape in
    # cell-templates-shacl.ttl, which is deliberately excluded from Tier 1's
    # merged-data validation (see EXAMPLE.md's Validation section) — asserting
    # sh:class here would spuriously fail against that merged graph. Most
    # template cells carry no cell:templateShape value at all — that's the
    # default.
    sh:property [
        sh:path cell:templateShape ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:message "A cell:TCell may have at most one cell:templateShape value."@en
    ] .


#################################################################
#  ACell
#  cell:ACell is the actual/instantiated facet of a cell (cell.ttl
#  3.7.0) — real, member-classified content. creator and memberCount
#  moved here from :CellShape when their domain narrowed from
#  cell:Cell to cell:ACell; subject and topics (renamed from
#  primary/secondary, themselves renamed from graph/sc-context)
#  moved here the same way in cell.ttl 3.10.0/3.12.0. As of cell.ttl
#  3.14.0/cell-shacl.ttl 3.12.0, cell:subject's and cell:topics's
#  per-member-count cardinality is no longer enforced uniformly here —
#  see :OneMemberShape/:TwoMemberShape/:ThreePlusMemberShape below.
#  :ACellShape retains only cell:subject's structural sh:nodeKind
#  check (applies regardless of member count) and cell:otherTopics's
#  unbounded, uniform constraint.
#################################################################

:ACellShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass cell:ACell ;
    sh:message "Actual Cell validation."@en ;

    # cell:subject — each value must be an IRI (not constrained to
    # sh:class topic:SCTopicGraph — its range widened to xsd:anyURI in
    # cell.ttl 3.12.0, since its values are the resource(s) the cell is
    # about, e.g. a p:Person/o:Organization, not a topic
    # container). Cardinality (exactly 1 vs 1..2) now varies by member
    # count — see :OneMemberShape/:TwoMemberShape/:ThreePlusMemberShape
    # below, not here.
    sh:property [
        sh:path cell:subject ;
        sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
        sh:message "A cell:ACell's cell:subject value(s) must each be an IRI."@en
    ] ;

    # cell:otherTopics — any number of additional topics beyond the
    # required cell:memberTopics baseline, each a topic:SCTopicGraph.
    # Optional and unbounded uniformly across all member counts, unlike
    # cell:memberTopics (see :OneMemberShape/:TwoMemberShape/
    # :ThreePlusMemberShape below). Split from cell:topics (cell.ttl up
    # to 3.13.0).
    sh:property [
        sh:path cell:otherTopics ;
        sh:class topic:SCTopicGraph ;
        sh:message "A cell:ACell's cell:otherTopics values, if present, must each be a topic:SCTopicGraph."@en
    ] ;

    # cell:creator — exactly one value, required, must be a Person or Organization
    sh:property [
        sh:path cell:creator ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:or ( [ sh:class p:Person ] [ sh:class o:Organization ] ) ;
        sh:message "A cell:ACell must have exactly one cell:creator, a single p:Person or o:Organization."@en
    ] ;

    # cell:memberCount — exactly one value, must be the class
    # cell:OneMember, cell:TwoMember, or cell:ThreePlusMember itself
    # (class-value punning, not a string). Required: every cell:ACell
    # instance is typed as one of these three by definition.
    sh:property [
        sh:path cell:memberCount ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:in ( cell:OneMember cell:TwoMember cell:ThreePlusMember ) ;
        sh:message "A cell:ACell's cell:memberCount is required and must be the class cell:OneMember, cell:TwoMember, or cell:ThreePlusMember."@en
    ] ;

    # cell:shape — at most one value. Not constrained to sh:class sh:NodeShape
    # here, for the same reason as cell:templateShape above: whatever shape
    # graph types the target as sh:NodeShape may not be part of the merged
    # data a given validation run includes. Most actual cells carry no
    # cell:shape value at all — that's the default.
    sh:property [
        sh:path cell:shape ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:message "A cell:ACell may have at most one cell:shape value."@en
    ] .


#################################################################
#  Per-Member-Count Shapes
#  cell:subject and cell:memberTopics both scale with how many total
#  members a cell:ACell individual represents (cell.ttl's Cell Member
#  Composition). Since yaml-to-rdf.py types every cell:ACell instance
#  with its concrete member class (cell:OneMember/cell:TwoMember/
#  cell:ThreePlusMember) in addition to asserting cell:memberCount, these
#  three shapes can target those classes directly via sh:targetClass.
#  cell:otherTopics is deliberately absent here — it stays uniform,
#  unbounded, and optional regardless of member count (see :ACellShape
#  above).
#################################################################

:OneMemberShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass cell:OneMember ;
    sh:message "OneMember Cell validation."@en ;

    sh:property [
        sh:path cell:subject ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:message "A cell:OneMember's cell:subject is required, exactly one value."@en
    ] ;

    sh:property [
        sh:path cell:memberTopics ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:class topic:SCTopicGraph ;
        sh:message "A cell:OneMember's cell:memberTopics is required, exactly one value, and it must be a topic:SCTopicGraph."@en
    ] .

:TwoMemberShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass cell:TwoMember ;
    sh:message "TwoMember Cell validation."@en ;

    sh:property [
        sh:path cell:subject ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:maxCount 2 ;
        sh:message "A cell:TwoMember's cell:subject is required, one or two values."@en
    ] ;

    sh:property [
        sh:path cell:memberTopics ;
        sh:minCount 2 ;
        sh:maxCount 4 ;
        sh:class topic:SCTopicGraph ;
        sh:message "A cell:TwoMember's cell:memberTopics is required, two to four values (one per self-vs-other combination), and each must be a topic:SCTopicGraph."@en
    ] .

:ThreePlusMemberShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass cell:ThreePlusMember ;
    sh:message "ThreePlusMember Cell validation."@en ;

    sh:property [
        sh:path cell:subject ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:message "A cell:ThreePlusMember's cell:subject is required, exactly one value."@en
    ] ;

    sh:property [
        sh:path cell:memberTopics ;
        sh:minCount 3 ;
        sh:class topic:SCTopicGraph ;
        sh:message "A cell:ThreePlusMember's cell:memberTopics is required, at least three values (one per member), and each must be a topic:SCTopicGraph."@en
    ] .
